  "IMPLEMENTED": [
    "Same original _RetainedSuspendedChild/API owns exact PROCESS_INFORMATION/call buffers before SDK entry, including original CreateProcess target, parent/profile/factory/role/Job and captured original native closers.",
    "Written outputs survive call/conversion failure. Unconfirmed/partial/malformed creation stays original-owner UNKNOWN; poll/wait/terminate/cleanup/new birth refuse. Only exact integer FALSE with all-zero original outputs permits a fresh owner attempt.",
    "Original process/thread outputs acquire actual original shared registry entries. Scope cleanup excludes child entries; their original closer checks exact binding/owner/lifecycle. Actual close/termination uncertainty is retained and cannot repeat an effect.",
    "The same original child survives confirmed suspension, Resume attempt, successful return and G2/finally/publication failure. No second owning return wrapper exists. G2 receipt is published after ancillary cleanup; getter signature/receipt fields are unchanged.",
    "Readonly observer bridge borrows genuine original process/thread/image entries. Pinned file adapter/closer is preserved; query adapter shares the registry, hashes/compares actual SDK file/mapping observations and releases only its own backing resource. No observation grants Resume authority.",
    "Successful Worker/Server returns transfer the same original child to the real consumer holder. Worker close separates never-resumed recovery from successful resumed retirement; UNKNOWN stays held with the existing startup latch. Server stop checks original holder before effects and releases only after exact HANDLE exit/listener absence.",
    "Known pre-SDK release deferrals may be reconciled only by the explicit original lifecycle owner after terminal facts. Arbitrary registry retries cannot impersonate it; actual possibly-effective close errors retain original acquisition without reclose.",
    "Normal termination refuses an unreturned Resume-UNKNOWN child; a copied ManagedServerHandle cannot terminate the original Server. Terminal release/registry/publication bookkeeping faults retain the same owner and source storage.",
    "Worker retains the exact original child/error pair only for a failed normal returned-owner retirement before process CloseHandle. Subsequent close can query that same original HANDLE and release only after exact terminal exit with intact original ownership, ACQUIRED process/RELEASED main-thread entries, no process release attempt and no retirement bookkeeping error. It cannot repeat terminate/kill/wait; start/RPC remain latched until confirmed release. Startup/readiness, unreturned Resume, creation, registry, close and bookkeeping UNKNOWN remain refused."
  ],
